%% OVERVIEW:
%%   Most LuaLaTeX documents load the 'fontspec' package, which is a front-end to 'luaotfload'.
%% That is a universal solution for describing and customizing any fonts from any compatible
%% technology, with any font language scripts.
%%   But Novelette provides its own fonts. No others may be used. These fonts were specifically
%% designed to work with Novelette. The software understands the fonts, and the fonts understand
%% how they will be used by the software. So there is no need for all that 'fontspec' offers.
%% What Novelette does need, has been simplified and written below. If you need decorative text
%% in another font, create it as a raster image.
%%   This page also contains some standard LaTeX command re-definitions, so that those commands
%% do it 'the Novelette way'. New commands are added, for text styles and OpenType features.


%% Cleanup:
